  "slug": "acid-nucleic-3d5f",
  "summary": "Recent preprints pair physics-informed scoring, language-model embeddings, and generative pipelines to improve binder ranking and design.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learned prediction and generation of molecular recognition interfaces that couple explicit structural information with sequence or language-model representations. ARID-sf combines force-field terms, structural features, and protein language model embeddings to rank antibody-antigen docking models, and Surf2Spot fuses sequence embeddings with structure and surface properties to predict PPI and nanobody-antigen hotspots. On the design side, TCRAD generates antigen-conditioned TCR CDR3beta sequences with filtration and structure prediction modules, and a separate benchmark evaluates staged generative peptide design across backbone generation and sequence design in TCR-pMHC complexes. DAGML extends geometric multimodal modeling to multi-domain protein-ligand affinity, encoding domain interfaces and linkers hierarchically. What is new is the multi-stage, multimodal architecture, in which structural, surface, and domain-level geometry are treated as explicit inputs alongside learned embeddings. All five entries are preprints and have not been peer reviewed.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-28"
}
